{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You love</b> — more. And some say: instead. But in this language we have not found it." "<b>Lie</b> — which he spoke, though Ahimelech knew that David was fleeing; therefore he was killed." "<b>You love</b> — the meaning is: you love evil."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {0 "The comment is elliptical; 'more' and 'instead' are proposed meanings for the form אהבת with no connective tissue added."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:39.695210262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}